--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this establishes
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

- regmap_config.reg_base carries the 0x800 value-element offset, so no
  custom regmap_bus is needed. The mainline SLIMbus backend already provides
  the 16-bit-register / 8-bit-value format this part requires.
- The translation is confirmed by comparison, not assumption: regmap and a
  direct slim_read of the same registers return identical bytes.
- 256 consecutive reads produced no errors and no drift.
- regmap is created inside device_status(UP), never in probe, because it
  rides on the logical address that device_up announces. A DOWN
  notification drops the reference.

This also exercises the regmap-slimbus backport. With the unfixed code the
managed path passes &slimbus -- the address of a stack parameter -- as the
bus context, so post-probe register access would dereference a dead stack
slot. Reads matching the direct path exactly is evidence the fix is doing
its job.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes and limits
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Kconfig cannot honour CONFIG_REGMAP_SLIMBUS=y here: SLIM_WCD9320_ENUM is
  a module and `select` from a tristate=m symbol forces the selected symbol
  to m. regmap-slimbus is therefore a module, and wcd9320-enum.ko records
  depends=regmap-slimbus. On a rootfs that predates it the dependency must
  be inserted first; the config has been corrected to =m so the file matches
  what is actually built.
- Caching is deliberately off. Volatility, power-on defaults and what
  survives a codec reset are still unmapped, and a cache that guesses any of
  those wrong is worse than none.
- NO write test was performed and no scratch register was invented. A write
  target must be demonstrably writable, unrelated to power, clocks, reset,
  interrupt acknowledgement and analog routing, not write-one-to-clear, and
  safe to restore. Writing a value back to an arbitrary control register is
  not automatically harmless.
- Two items from the milestone's proof list are NOT covered here: that a
  codec reset produces clean absence and re-enumeration, and that regmap is
  safely recreated afterwards. The DOWN path depends on
  slim_report_absent(), which nothing currently calls, so that needs a
  deliberate mechanism rather than a module unload.
